{"name":"Bourgeois","hex":"#ee0066","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Bourgeois","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname from French."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Bourgeois"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bourgeoisie","blocks":[{"text":"The bourgeoisie are a social class of business owners, merchants and wealthy people, in general, which emerged in the Late Middle Ages, originally as a \"middle class\" between the peasantry and aristocracy. They are traditionally contrasted with the proletariat by their wealth, political power, and education, as well as their access to and control of cultural, social, and financial capital."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Jean_B%C3%A9raud_-_La_Sortie_du_Bourgeois.jpg/330px-Jean_B%C3%A9raud_-_La_Sortie_du_Bourgeois.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bourgeoisie","wikidata":"Q52090"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Fuggerkontor.jpg/500px-Fuggerkontor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Fuggerkontor.jpg/1280px-Fuggerkontor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Fuggerkontor.jpg/500px-Fuggerkontor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The 16th-century German banker Jakob Fugger and his principal accountant, M. Schwarz, registering an entry to a ledger. The background shows a file cabinet indicating the European cities where the Fugger bank conducts business (1517).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFuggerkontor.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Karl_Marx_001.jpg/500px-Karl_Marx_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=pars